WEBVTT

NOTE
English translation of a short Bible-translation review conducted in Japanese
and Korean. The opening paraphrases John 9:31; the final exchange compares word
choices across translations.

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.000
[Japanese] God does not listen to sinners.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
[Japanese] But when someone worships God and does what God wills,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
[Japanese] God listens to that person.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[Korean] Is that rendered as “worship” there?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
[Korean] Yes, as “worship.”

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
[Korean] What wording does the Russian translation use?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.000
[Korean] Yes. Yes.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
[Korean] Then let’s examine the word “reverence” from earlier.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.040
[Korean] No, there it says “reverence” …
